WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.245
Privacy and data protection are operational requirements, not afterthoughts. Multi-jurisdiction intelligence work can involve personal data, sensitive business data, partner information, telemetry, fraud records, incident notes, or regulated records.

2
00:00:12.365 --> 00:00:17.671
The team has to protect that material while still producing useful decision support.

3
00:00:17.791 --> 00:00:24.730
Data minimization is the discipline of collecting and sharing only what is necessary for the authorized purpose.

4
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:30.156
It starts before collection begins and continues through analysis, dissemination, retention, and closure.

5
00:00:30.276 --> 00:00:40.888
If the decision can be supported without names, exact locations, full account identifiers, raw messages, or unrestricted logs, those details should be removed, generalized, or protected.

6
00:00:41.008 --> 00:00:48.763
More data is not always better. Unnecessary data can increase compliance burden, create avoidable exposure, and make sharing harder.

7
00:00:48.883 --> 00:00:55.822
Common privacy controls include redaction, aggregation, pseudonymization, access control, approved storage, retention limits, and careful product design.

8
00:00:55.942 --> 00:01:02.473
Redaction removes details that the audience does not need. Aggregation shows patterns without exposing individual records.

9
00:01:02.593 --> 00:01:09.123
Pseudonymization can support analysis while limiting direct identification. Access control limits who can view sensitive records.

10
00:01:09.243 --> 00:01:15.366
Retention rules prevent intelligence workspaces from becoming permanent stores of data that should have expired.

11
00:01:15.486 --> 00:01:20.792
Privacy also affects dissemination. A technical team may need an affected system list.

12
00:01:20.912 --> 00:01:27.442
A partner may need a sanitized indicator summary. An executive may need risk and recommended action.

13
00:01:27.562 --> 00:01:35.726
A legal reviewer may need source, authority, and handling context. These audiences do not all need the same raw material.

14
00:01:35.846 --> 00:01:41.560
Tailoring the product reduces risk and improves usefulness. Data protection includes storage and movement.

15
00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:48.211
Use approved systems, approved sharing channels, markings, and documented access. Avoid informal channels for sensitive information.

16
00:01:48.331 --> 00:01:56.902
If cross-border sharing, employee data, customer data, government reporting, or contractual restrictions are involved, route the issue to qualified reviewers.

17
00:01:57.022 --> 00:02:06.818
The safest intelligence product answers the decision question with the least sensitive detail necessary, clear caveats, and a record of how privacy was considered.
